id: pm-szn67i
title: "Review hardening: terminator-safe recovery, exact nested aliases, and tracker-scoped close retries"
description: "Resolve the coupled CodeRabbit findings on the broad SDK agent command contract PR: missing-option recovery must preserve argv terminator semantics, item addressing must expose --id only for the declared item complete subcommand, and strict-close recovery must retain the explicitly selected tracker path."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk","pr:957",recovery,review-followup
created_at: "2026-08-09T22:41:16.367Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-09T23:09:02.855Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-09T23:09:02.373Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-09T23:09:02.373Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Recovery inserts missing flags before argv terminator and preserves trailing operands; Only item complete accepts the nested --id compatibility alias; Strict-close recovery preserves selected --pm-path/--path tracker scope; Focused regression tests and exact-head quality gates pass
definition_of_ready: Three concrete review findings reproduced against PR #957 and no all-status duplicate found.
value: Keep public SDK recovery primitives trustworthy for agent automation.
impact: Prevents incorrect retries and cross-workspace mutation risk.
outcome: All three review findings resolved through SDK-first behavior with regression coverage.
why_now: PR #957 review is active and must reach a clean exact head before merge.
parent: pm-usfg
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: PR #957 exact head 5e19c578b
repro_steps: Review renderMissingOptionRetry with argv containing --; normalize item --id without complete; trigger strict close with a tracker selected outside cwd.
resolution: "Missing options are inserted before argv terminators, nested-only item aliases require the declared subcommand while dual-mode files remains compatible, and strict-close recovery renders an absolute canonical --pm-path."
expected_result: "Generated retry commands remain executable against the intended command and tracker, and nested aliases only apply to declared subcommands."
actual_result: "Focused 84-test tranche and full 7,110-test suite pass; coverage is 100/100/100/100; lint, duplication, docstrings, static quality, tracker measurements, and temporary cross-cwd acceptance pass."
component: SDK agent primitives and lifecycle recovery
regression: true
customer_impact: Agents can receive a retry that changes parse semantics or mutates the wrong project tracker.
