comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-09T22:41:16.367Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: searched all 2,397 items and fully read the only detector candidate pm-xg60q3. That closed chore owns a coverage-shard timing repair in a different integration test; this item owns three newly reported production recovery/address defects, so explicit duplicate override is justified. Canonical implementation lineage remains pm-p316vn, pm-mkinft, pm-ulqu, and pm-usfg."
  "2026-08-09T22:48:45.901Z","harness:codex","Coverage evidence: the first repo-wide run executed 7,110 tests and found one integration regression in files --id. Root cause: the initial nested-subcommand guard treated files (which is both a direct item command and a discover namespace) like item (which is nested-only). No product mutation escaped; correcting the SDK capability distinction before rerun."
  "2026-08-09T22:57:43.146Z","harness:codex","Quality-gate evidence: lint exposed complexity added by representing direct+nested command capability inline, so the grammar decision is now isolated in a documented resolver used for both pre- and post-normalization indices. Tracker measurement also caught the PR-957 title prefix as a third duplicate issue-code group; the item title now describes the defect class while PR provenance remains in tags/environment/comments."
  "2026-08-09T23:09:01.449Z","harness:codex","Final evidence: manual /tmp acceptance proved strict-close recovery from an unrelated cwd retained the selected tracker and executed to a successful strict close. Focused SDK/CLI tests pass 84/84. The final repository coverage run passes 7,110/7,110 with statements 50,794/50,794, branches 37,162/37,162, functions 10,435/10,435, and lines 49,146/49,146. pnpm lint and quality:static pass, including zero clones, 100% docstrings, SDK surface, transport floors, token/context gates, and tracker measurement ratchets."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-09T22:41:16.367Z","harness:codex",Scope is deliberately one coupled review-hardening tranche because all three defects concern executable recovery/address contracts exposed through the new public SDK surface.
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-09T22:41:16.367Z","harness:codex",Review follow-ups that alter public command construction require both token-vector tests and a manual invocation from a workspace different from the selected tracker.
  "2026-08-09T23:09:01.830Z","harness:codex","Capability tables must distinguish commands that are direct-only, nested-only, or dual-mode; sharing a subcommand map alone is insufficient. Recovery commands should carry the resolved absolute tracker root, not rely on the caller remaining in the same workspace."
